  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoder choice is the strongest lever so far—pca_n2000 (config_002, 0.591) vs scvi_n200 (config_005, 0.650) with identical multiprofile/avgpool setup shows a ~6-point gain. scgpt is completely untested. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable A/B against config_005, isolating whether scgpt matches, exceeds, or underperforms scvi_n200. Why best next: the RNA encoder is the most fundamental design axis and propagates into every multimodal configuration; resolving this uncertainty before further multimodal/fusion experiments avoids wasting budget on suboptimal encoder choices. If scgpt is clearly superior, all subsequent multimodal tests should use it; if similar or worse, we can confidently commit to scvi_n200 and pivot to fusion-method or image-encoder questions."
}

